# Down by the riverside - spiritual en kampvuurlied
# Afro-Amerikaanse spiritual met wortels van vóór de Amerikaanse Burgeroorlog; eerste druk
# 1918 in Plantation Melodies (Rodeheaver Company, Chicago), eerste opname 1920 door het
# Fisk University jubilee quartet (Wikipedia (en), "Down by the Riverside"). Publiek domein.
# Overgenomen uit DOWN_BY.RIV (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991) en Down by the riverside.doc
# (Word 97-2003, 2005); beide teksten zijn gelijk. Het eerste couplet en het refrein, met
# akkoorden, komen uit het WordPerfect-bestand (uitlijning met spaties); de overige
# coupletten uit het Word-bestand, waar twee regels niet aan elkaar vastzitten.
# De bron geeft de latere coupletten verkort met "......" (zingen als het eerste couplet);
# zo overgenomen. Het refrein staat in de bron eenmaal, met "(2x)"; hier na elk couplet.
{title: Down by the riverside}
{meta: id down-by-the-riverside}
{meta: language en}
{lyricist: traditioneel}
{composer: traditioneel}
{year: 1918}
{copyright: Public domain}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: source Overgenomen uit DOWN_BY.RIV (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991) en Down by the riverside.doc (2005); herkomst via Wikipedia (en)}
{meta: tag kampvuur}
{meta: tag geestelijk}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna lay [C]down my burden,
down by the riverside
down [G]by the riverside
down [C]by the riverside
Gonna lay down my burden,
down by the riverside
[G]to study war no [C]more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrein (2x)}
I ain't [F]gonna study war no more
I ain't [C]gonna study war no more
I [G]ain't gonna study [C]war no more
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna lay down my sword and shield ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna try on my long white robe ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna ride in the gold chariot ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna try on my starry crown ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna climb the road to Heaven ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
I'll fight the wicked devil ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna climb upon that mountain ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna cross the river of Jordan ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna read the Holy Bible ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna meet my blessed Jesus ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna walk with the Prince of Peace ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna shake hands around the world ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna put on my traveling shoes ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
Gonna put on my starry crown ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
I met my little bright eyed doll ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
I asked her for a little kiss ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
She said have patience little man
I'm sure you'll understand
I hardly know your name .......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
I said if I can have my way
Maybe some sweet day
My name and yours will be the same ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}

{start_of_verse}
I wed my little bright eyed doll ......
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Refrein (2x)}
